  "result": "Excellent! All 201 tests pass! Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Added optional `terms` parameter to `createInvoice()` (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Imported `addDays` from dates module for term calculations\n- Added terms validation with three supported options:\n  - **NET14**: Due 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: Due 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - **EOM**: Due on the last day of the issue date's month\n- Calculates `dueDate` based on terms and issueDate\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on created invoice\n- Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n\n**Key calculation logic:**\n- **NET14/NET30**: Uses `addDays()` to calculate future date\n- **EOM**: Calculates last day of issue month using UTC date operations\n- Correctly handles leap years and month boundaries\n- All date arithmetic in UTC (never local timezone)\n\n**Added 12 comprehensive tests in `test/invoices.test.js`:**\n- Default NET30 terms\n- NET14 term calculation\n- NET30 term calculation\n- EOM calculation for mid-month issue dates\n- EOM calculation for start-of-month issue dates\n- EOM calculation for end-of-month issue dates (same day)\n- TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n- Leap year handling (Feb 29 in 2024)\n- Non-leap year handling (Feb 28 in 2025)\n- Year boundary handling (NET14 and NET30 crossing year)\n\n**Examples of calculated due dates:**\n- Issue: 2025-02-14, NET14 \u2192 Due: 2025-02-28\n- Issue: 2025-02-14, NET30 \u2192 Due: 2025-03-16\n- Issue: 2025-02-14, EOM \u2192 Due: 2025-02-28\n- Issue: 2024-12-25, NET14 \u2192 Due: 2025-01-08 (year boundary)\n\nAll 201 tests pass! \u2713",
